sec.p:
Figure 2c–e illustrates the performance of each model type (ANN, GNN, and combined) across different mass bins (see also Supplementary Fig. S2 for details about each individual ANN model). We evaluate performance using accuracy and the F1 score (see Methods section for details). Due to the unbalanced nature of the target values—where even the most frequent peaks are relatively rare—accuracy often approaches 1 and does not provide a clear picture of model performance. In contrast, the F1 score, which is close to both precision and recall because our models are well-calibrated, is more informative. Our results show that the ANN and combined models, with mean F1 scores of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
