To validate the performance of SingleFrag at the task of annotating spectra, we use the same test set of molecules as in previous sections. For each MS/MS spectrum, we generate a list of candidate molecules with compatible molecular formulas (Fig. 4a and d) or compatible molecular masses, assuming a spectrometer precision of either 1ppm (Fig. 4b and e) or 10ppm (Fig. 4c and f). We evaluate the annotation performance by tracking the position of the true molecule in the candidate ranking for each test molecule. In Fig. 4a-c, we show the frequency with which the true molecule is ranked first (Top 1, indicating perfect annotation), among the top five candidates (Top 5), and among the top ten candidates (Top 10). We measure this performance under four experimental conditions: using low (0–14 eV), medium (15–39 eV), or high (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
