${^{-4}}$\end{document}, and binary cross entropy as the loss function. We set a minimum of 200 and a maximum of 2000 epochs for training, and keep the model with the lowest validation loss. We also implemented an early auto-stop if the validation loss increased while the training loss decreased, comparing the most recent epoc to the previous 100 epochs.

sec.p:
Because the training and test sets are selected at random, the expected fraction of molecules having a peak in a specific m/z bin in the train, validation and test sets is the same. Therefore we have to select a threshold that recovers the statistically correct fraction of molecules with peaks in that bin. To that end, for a specific m/z bin, we rank the \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
